  m_Name: Q3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HistoricalQuestionData
  questionID: Q3
  questionText: "According to legend, which deity gave An D\u01B0\u01A1ng V\u01B0\u01A1ng
    claws to make the magic crossbow?"
  answers:
  - Golden Dragon
  - Lac Bird
  - Golden Turtle God
  - Giao Long
  correctAnswerIndex: 0
  answerFeedbacks:
  - Wrong! The Golden Dragon (Hoang Long) is a symbol of the power of kings and emperors,
    not the one who bestowed the magic crossbow.
  - Wrong! The Lac Bird is the totem of the ancient Vietnamese people, often depicted
    on Dong Son bronze drums.
  - Exactly! The divine crossbow was made from the claws of the Golden Turtle God.
  - Wrong! Giao Long is a mythical sea monster; ancient Vietnamese people had to
    tattoo themselves to avoid being harmed by it.
  difficultyTier: 1
